{"open_points":[{"subject":"model_fields.model_items model recognition","kind":"missing_boundary_guarantee","unit":"context","text":"For a model, its declared fields as name and value pairs in their declared order, a nested model given as a value and not opened; for any other value, that it is no model.","question":"Must the public contract state that every instance of pydantic's BaseModel is a model, including subclasses not declared in module:models, and that no other value is a model?","options":["Treat every pydantic BaseModel instance as a model.","Treat only classes declared by module:models as models.","Leave recognition to each caller."],"default_guess":"Treat every pydantic BaseModel instance as a model, as the received State 3 decision requires.","witness":{"initial":"A caller passes an instance of a pydantic BaseModel subclass that is not declared by module:models.","events":["module:service_api calls model_fields.model_items with that instance."],"outcomes":["model_items returns the instance's declared name-value pairs.","model_items answers that the value is no model."],"observer":"module:service_api and the service receiving its wire answer"}},{"subject":"model_fields.model_items non-model result","kind":"vague_result","unit":"50_public_apis_0_conventions.md","text":"for any other value, that it is no model.","question":"What result may callers rely on to distinguish a non-model from a model with no declared fields?","options":["Return None for every non-model, as the received State 3 decision states.","Return a tagged non-model result.","Return an empty collection and require callers to distinguish it by another rule."],"default_guess":"Return None for every non-model.","witness":{"initial":"A caller passes an ordinary value, and an empty pydantic model is also possible.","events":["module:operations calls model_fields.model_items for each value and branches only on its answer."],"outcomes":["The ordinary value returns None while the empty model returns an empty collection, so they are distinct.","Both return an empty collection, so the caller cannot distinguish them from the answer alone."],"observer":"module:operations when classifying an answer"}},{"subject":"imports.internal model_fields export surface","kind":"incomplete_export_surface","unit":"50_public_apis_0_conventions.md","text":"and `imports.internal["model_fields"]` exports it.","question":"Is model_items the complete public export surface of module:model_fields, or may that module expose additional symbols?","options":["Declare `imports.internal["model_fields"]` as containing `model_items` alone.","Permit additional public exports and enumerate them before State 6 writes the complete surface."],"default_guess":"Declare `model_items` alone, matching the sole public operation under review.","witness":{"initial":"State 6 must materialize the complete imports.internal entry for model_fields.","events":["One careful writer treats “exports it” as membership only.","Another treats the sole public operation as the entire export surface."],"outcomes":["The entry contains model_items plus an additional public helper.","The entry contains only model_items."],"observer":"The slicer and any generated consumer determining the provider's public API"}},{"subject":"pydantic import catalog entry","kind":"later_layer_choice","unit":"context","text":"It imports pydantic's base model class as the third-party import `from pydantic import BaseModel`, declared as `imports.third_party_by_module["model_fields"]`; no other module imports it.","question":"How will State 6 record this required module-scoped import in the global third-party import catalog required by SPEC_STANDARD §7?","decision_owner":"6","options":["Add `from pydantic import BaseModel` to global `imports.third_party` and to `imports.third_party_by_module["model_fields"]`.","Record only the module-scoped row and assume it need not also be admitted by the global catalog."],"consequences":["The import is both globally admitted and structurally assigned to model_fields.","The module-scoped need is recorded, but a later validator or generator may reject it as absent from the catalog of permitted third-party imports."],"requirement":"It imports pydantic's base model class as the third-party import `from pydantic import BaseModel`, declared as `imports.third_party_by_module["model_fields"]`; no other module imports it.","default_guess":"Add the full import string to both the global catalog and the model_fields module-scoped row."},{"subject":"model_fields reflection procedure","kind":"later_layer_choice","unit":"context","text":"### Hides

pydantic's reflection API: how a model's declared fields and their order are
found.","question":"Which supported pydantic reflection procedure and version assumption will implement the walk without changing its boundary behaviour?","decision_owner":"7","options":["Pin the selected pydantic major version and use its supported declared-field API.","Implement a compatibility adapter for every pydantic major version the generated project supports."],"consequences":["Pinning gives one smaller implementation but ties the generated project to that pydantic API.","An adapter supports more dependency versions but adds compatibility branches and tests."],"requirement":"Reading the declared fields of a model value — each field's name and value, in the order the model declares them — and telling a model from any other value","default_guess":"Pin one supported pydantic major version and use its public declared-field API."}]}
